          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "मयूरः (mayūraḥ) — \"a peacock\", who dances when the वर्षा comes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of mayūra is disputed. CDIAL 9865 reports three proposals: a Dravidian source (compare Tamil mayil, DEDR 4642), an Austroasiatic one, and an old Indo-Iranian colour word. It lives on as Hindi mor, \"peacock\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The dancing bird."
